Ladybird drops an extension’s privacy settings when it’s removed,
disabled, reloaded, or loses the privacy permission, and announces the
value then in effect. Firefox removes an extension’s settings on
uninstall, and when the permission that granted them is revoked, in
ExtensionPreferencesManager.removeSettingsForPermissions(); Chromium’s
ExtensionPrefValueMap drops an unloaded extension’s values too.
